    "updated_at": "2021-02-25T14:39:30Z",
    "body": "I guess there is at least one thing here to act on which is what should happen when you remove the newline after \"sad\" (i.e., no newlines at all after headers). At that point Firefox starts acting funny and is seemingly non-deterministic, Safari network errors the response, and Chrome keeps trucking. I created tests that expect a network error for this, as Safari already does, and filed bugs:\r\n\r\n* https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/27456\r\n* https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1690481, follow-up: https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1694361\r\n* https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=1173975\r\n\r\nReview welcome!",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
